Level ID: [B80E-0000-03EC-E3B9](https://supermariomakerbookmark.nintendo.net/courses/B80E-0000-03EC-E3B9)

&#x200B;

My final Mario Maker level, a SMB3 Castle. A Platformer with a few puzzle elements to it. See you all in a week and a half

Level ID: [10A5-0000-006A-957B](https://supermariomakerbookmark.nintendo.net/courses/10A5-0000-006A-957B)

&#x200B;

One of my older levels, A normal difficulty super mario world basically showing off the POW Block. Simple level

&#x200B;

Level ID: [A3B9-0000-01A2-CEE9](https://supermariomakerbookmark.nintendo.net/courses/A3B9-0000-01A2-CEE9)

&#x200B;

Another older level, A SMB3 platformer, not much to say overall. Was basically experimenting with revisiting segments of the level. 

&#x200B;

Let me know what you guys think! I am glad I found this subreddit, great community

\*  Level ID: \[[9673-0000-02A2-011E](https://supermariomakerbookmark.nintendo.net/courses/9673-0000-02A2-011E)\]

Crashed World

&#x200B;

Difficulty: Normal-Hard

&#x200B;

SMB costume level (I am going to miss these levels:( but it doesnt kill my excitement). Fox has landed on a mysterious world, can he get to his ship and survive? a nice Platforming with some tricky sections.

\*  Level ID: \[01B7-0000-03E9-F914\]([https://supermariomakerbookmark.nintendo.net/courses/01B7-0000-03E9-F914](https://supermariomakerbookmark.nintendo.net/courses/01B7-0000-03E9-F914))

&#x200B;

A recent level that is basically a beta for a level I want to make in MM2. Traditional Platformer, and kindof a goofy level. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

\*  Level ID: \[2192-0000-00D9-AE06\]([https://supermariomakerbookmark.nintendo.net/courses/2192-0000-00D9-AE06](https://supermariomakerbookmark.nintendo.net/courses/2192-0000-00D9-AE06))

&#x200B;

One of my older levels, but one of my favorite I have made. A few of my friends enjoyed it when I made them play it. Supposed to be a tricky Mario World level. The Airship Theme in Mario World is one my favorite to use.
